[size=4][b][color=#FF6A1A]Kilnwarden 0.1.0: the first release[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]A web admin panel for your Enshrouded dedicated server, served over HTTPS from inside the server. Needs [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/enshrouded/mods/301][color=#F9C74F]Kiln[/color][/url] 0.2.0-dev.31.10 or later on the server; players need nothing.[/color][/size]

[list]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]The Kiln Launcher's admin pages in any browser, every command as a form, player activity, schedules, mod switches and checked updates with rollback, metrics with alerts, webhooks, roles with two-factor sign-in, an audit log and an optional public page.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Starts closed: it answers only on the server's machine until you have an owner account and open it up in Panel settings. Routes for home, VPS, rented game servers, Docker and CGNAT: [url=https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kilnwarden/blob/main/docs/hosting-routes.md][color=#F9C74F]the guide[/color][/url].[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Hosted access at [b]<name>.kiln.nexus[/b] is coming soon (no port forwarding, never decrypted by frostdev): the panel side is in this release, and the relay goes live soon.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]The Kiln Launcher's [b]Open web panel[/b] shows for Kilnwarden from Kiln 0.2.0-dev.31.14 (coming soon); until then, use the setup link from kiln.log.[/color][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Ran a Kiln Web Admin test build? Delete [b]kiln/mods/kiln-webadmin/[/b] first; Kilnwarden moves your data from [b]kiln/data/kiln-webadmin/[/b] at its first start.[/color][/size][/*]
[/list]
[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]File: kilnwarden-0.1.0.zip, sha256 [b]7d9b98567e30274ad7b4332c6c1ca68bee4736d637446332e83634e854c7b6b0[/b]. Source and a reproducible build: [url=https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kilnwarden][color=#F9C74F]GitHub[/color][/url].[/color][/size]

[size=3][color=#D4D4D8]Bugs and ideas: [url=https://discord.gg/7pjr8SMTfU][color=#F9C74F]Kiln Discord[/color][/url] (#bug-reports) or the Bugs tab, with [b]kiln/logs/kiln.log[/b]. Security problems: privately, please (GitHub's "Report a vulnerability", or a direct message to a moderator on Discord).[/color][/size]
